            <ArticleTitle>A case of missed blunt traumatic aortic injury (BTAI).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>193-194</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We are reporting a case of missed blunt traumatic aortic injury (BTAI). A 28 year male presented with chest pain following a motor vehicle accident. He was discharged following normal clinical signs and chest radiograph. The following day he complained of lower limb weakness. Traumatic aortic dissection was revealed via computer tomography (CT) of the thorax. BTAI cannot be ruled out with normal clinical signs and chest radiograph alone. CT thorax is mandatory to rule out BTAI in high impact chest injury.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
